From: Midgy BALON <midgy971@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3568-rock-3b: Enable NPU with
 Rocket driver

Enable the RK3568 NPU on the Radxa ROCK 3B board.  The NPU is fed from
vdd_npu (825–1000 mV range), with clock rates of 1 GHz (SCMI/PVTPLL)
and 600 MHz (CRU divider), matching the 1000 mV operating point.

Rename the supply property from the BSP-specific "rknpu-supply" to the
"npu-supply" property required by the binding.

Drop "operating-points-v2": the Rocket driver does not implement devfreq
and the OPP table is not part of the rknn-core binding schema.

Enable the NPU IOMMU (rknpu_mmu) so the Rocket driver can create a
per-file IOMMU domain for DMA isolation.

Signed-off-by: Midgy BALON <midgy971@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-rock-3b.dts | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-rock-3b.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-rock-3b.dts
index XXXXXXX..XXXXXXX 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-rock-3b.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-rock-3b.dts
@@ -809,10 +809,8 @@
 
 &rknpu {
 	assigned-clocks = <&scmi_clk SCMI_CLK_NPU>, <&cru CLK_NPU>;
 	assigned-clock-rates = <1000000000>, <600000000>;
-	operating-points-v2 = <&npu_opp_table>;
-	rknpu-supply = <&vdd_npu>;
+	npu-supply = <&vdd_npu>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &rknpu_mmu {
 	status = "okay";
 };
